From: Lars Wikman <lars@underjord.io>
Date: Fri, 10 Oct 2026 15:10:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] leds: trigger: pattern: initialise repeat for hardware patterns

pattern_trig_activate() marks a fresh trigger as indefinite and makes
the repeat attribute read -1, but leaves data->repeat itself at 0.
Software patterns never look at repeat while is_indefinite is set, so
nobody noticed. A hardware pattern, though, passes data->repeat straight
to the driver's pattern_set(), and leds-qcom-lpg accepts only -1 and 1
there: on a PMI632 every write to hw_pattern fails with EINVAL until
userspace first writes the -1 to repeat that the attribute already
claims to hold.

Initialise repeat together with last_repeat.
---
 drivers/leds/trigger/ledtrig-pattern.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/leds/trigger/ledtrig-pattern.c b/drivers/leds/trigger/ledtrig-pattern.c
--- a/drivers/leds/trigger/ledtrig-pattern.c
+++ b/drivers/leds/trigger/ledtrig-pattern.c
@@ -478,7 +478,7 @@
 
 	data->type = PATTERN_TYPE_SW;
 	data->is_indefinite = true;
-	data->last_repeat = -1;
+	data->last_repeat = data->repeat = -1;
 	mutex_init(&data->lock);
 	data->led_cdev = led_cdev;
 	led_set_trigger_data(led_cdev, data);
